 "resumeFix": "P1.1 fix in pipeline/src/services/feed/trace.ts createFeedTraceRecorder: added a per-index `hydrated: boolean[]` array parallel to `calls`/`payloads`. Calls recorded this process are marked hydrated=true immediately (their in-memory payload is already whatever record() received, even if that happens to be undefined on an error path -- nothing left to read). A restored (resume) call starts hydrated=false; a new `hydratedPayload(index)` helper lazily reads and JSON.parses `join(runDir, call.payload_path)` on first access via `recordedCalls()`, caches the result in `payloads[index]`, and marks it hydrated so repeat calls never re-read the file. Missing or unparseable payload files are caught and skipped (payload stays undefined), never thrown. recordedCalls() now calls `hydratedPayload(i)` instead of returning `payloads[i]` directly. No change was needed in feed-refs.ts buildFeedRefsUniverse -- it already consumes recorder.recordedCalls(), so it now resolves restored chunk_refs/article_refs/text automatically once the recorder hydrates them.",
